From 119019414f237ca035dfc347837f7ea4727f337c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gillinger <christian.gillinger@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:07:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] genesys: frame selection and magazine handling for the
 OpticFilm 135i

Five options, inactive on every other ASIC: 'frame' (which frame of the
loaded strip to scan, 1-6, the geometry being fixed by the holder);
'load-film', which releases the magazine, waits for the loader sensor
to see it taken out and pushed back in, and then loads it, all in one
press, since SANE cannot prompt during sane_start; 'eject-film';
'check-status', which re-reads the hardware; and a 'magazine' status
line telling the operator the next step. A scan never loads the
magazine itself: with nothing loaded, sane_start refuses read-only.
The magazine state survives across processes through a mark file next
to the process lock, and sane_open/sane_close take the companion
driver's process lock around the device.

Options that the GL126 hooks do not implement are inactive for it, so
a frontend shows only what the scanner does.
